cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Anchored Targeted Projection Pursuit — reference implementation and
  reproduction package
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this record) and
  the accompanying article.
type: software
version: 3.2.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of anchored targeted projection pursuit (anchored
  TPP), a closed-form, hyperparameter-free method for hypothesis-driven quality
  control of multivariate geochemical data from a small set of analyst-selected
  anchor samples. Includes the fully synthetic XRF core-scan benchmark
  generator, the semi-synthetic experiment pipeline, comparison baselines
  (PCA, single-element rules, MCD, isolation forest, one-class SVM, positive
  unlabeled logistic regression), and scripts reproducing every figure and
  reported value in the accompanying article.
keywords:
  - projection pursuit
  - geochemical data quality control
  - mineral exploration
  - XRF core scanning
  - compositional data analysis
  - anomaly detection
  - orthogonal Procrustes
